## Step 4: Infrastructure & Input Handling (Platform-wide)
Focus on RCE, Injections, SSRF, and XXE ($750–$3,000 payouts). [11, 12] 

* Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF):
* Identify fields that load external data (e.g., loading profile pictures from a URL, adding external RSS feeds, or webhook integrations).
   * Change the URL to target internal infrastructure (e.g., http://127.0.0.1:80 or cloud metadata endpoints like http://169.254.169.254). Non-blind readable SSRF pays $1,300.
* File Uploads (LFR / RFI / XXE):
* If the platform allows document uploads for KYC verification (ID/Passport copies), test the upload mechanism.
   * Upload malicious XML files inside SVG or DOCX formats to test for XML External Entity (XXE) injection.
   * Attempt to upload a web shell (e.g., .php, .jsp) disguised as an image to achieve Remote Code Execution (RCE). [13] 

