## Phase 3: Reporting Requirements
If you find a valid vulnerability, ensure your report meets the submission standard to avoid delays: [14, 15] 

   1. Written Description: Clearly explain the vulnerability and its real-world impact.
   2. Step-by-Step Replication: Write clean, concise steps. Do not rely solely on video/images.
   3. Proof of Concept (PoC): Provide the exact request payload or script used to trigger the bug.
   4. No Post-Exploitation: Once you prove the bug exists (e.g., reading a benign system file name via XXE), stop immediately. Do not attempt to download sensitive database content. [16, 17, 18, 19, 20] 

